  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.4.0: Security — the net8.0-windows dependencies System.Security.Cryptography.Xml and System.Management move from 9.0.17 to 10.0.12. 9.0.0-9.0.17 carry GHSA-23rf-6693-g89p and four sibling advisories. The assembly still targets net8.0-windows (the 10.0.x packages ship a lib/net8.0 asset), so consumers do NOT need .NET 10 and nothing changes for the net481 build. New offline test project LicenseManagement.EndUser.Net8.Tests pins signature verification with frozen vectors signed under the old stack. 3.2.0: Additive — CompactLicense.FetchAsync + LicenseFormat (jws / es256 / eddsa) to fetch the compact JWS license for embedded / non-.NET consumers. The XML activation flow is unchanged. 3.0.1: Bug fixes — LicenseHandlingUninstall reads from disk (not install chain); LicenseSignatureValidationHandler now correctly distinguishes tampered files from key rotation (throws CryptographicException on tamper). 3.0.0: Audit-driven hardening release. Centralized HTTP plumbing (15s timeout, retry-with-backoff for 429/503, Retry-After honoring, Idempotency-Key on POST, X-Correlation-Id, RFC 7807 problem+json error parsing). Hardened XML signature validation (XmlResolver=null, public-key shape check). Typed exceptions instead of base Exception. ILicenseLogger interface for observability. PublisherPreferences.ToString() masks ApiKey. ConfigureAwait(false) applied consistently. Several public infrastructure types are now internal (LicenseValidationHandler, *ApiEndPoint, MainRegistryKeyIn*, NullDeviceIdFormatter). See CHANGELOG.md for full list.",
